cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Sw-SSFCM_Dataset — benchmark scenes, label-budget splits and guidance-scale parameters
message: >-
  If you use these splits or the loader, please cite both this dataset record
  and the accompanying paper listed under preferred-citation.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Nguyen
    given-names: Xuan Hoang
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0007-1721-6931
  - family-names: Mai
    given-names: Dinh Sinh
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7284-5713
  - family-names: Nguyen
    given-names: Long Giang
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6184-1469
repository-code: https://github.com/longlinh/Sw-SSFCM_Dataset
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22085053
abstract: >-
  Reproducibility kit for the label-budget protocol of Sw-SSFCM on six public
  hyperspectral benchmarks (Botswana, Kennedy Space Center, Indian Pines, Pavia
  University, Houston 2013, WHU-Hi-LongKou): retrieval scripts, a self-contained
  Python loader, the 300 canonical semi-supervised splits (6 scenes x 5 label
  budgets x 10 draws) and the guidance-scale parameters of the theta-rule. The
  hyperspectral cubes themselves remain with their original providers.
keywords:
  - hyperspectral image classification
  - semi-supervised clustering
  - fuzzy c-means
  - label budget
  - remote sensing
  - reproducibility
